---
title: Shell request path and window-close lifecycle (implemented)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant View as egui frame (Shell::ui)
  participant Client as Client (worker threads)
  participant BE as DesktopBackend
  participant RT as Runtime
  participant Eng as Engine thread
  View->>Client: command(Slot::Append(session), sessions.append_message frame)
  Client->>BE: on a worker: command(op, frame)
  BE->>RT: Runtime::command(user context, op, frame)
  RT-->>BE: CommandOutcome
  BE-->>Client: Reply::Command
  Client-->>View: waker → request_repaint
  View->>Client: poll() — superseded replies for the same slot are dropped
  View->>View: apply: update the draft, transcript projection, status (live region)
  Eng-->>View: dispatcher hint (watch) → re-query what is visible (transcript after its tail cursor)
  Note over View: window close button
  View->>View: CancelClose, Lifecycle Open → Quiescing (Client closed to new requests)
  View->>Client: wait for in-flight requests (bounded 10 s)
  View->>View: Persisting — ui-state.json written
  View->>Eng: HostControl::begin_shutdown
  Eng->>RT: Runtime::shutdown — stop delivery, collection, housekeeping, wait in-flight deliveries, stop owned trees within one bound, release keep-awake
  Eng-->>View: poll_shutdown() → summary
  View->>View: Exiting → ViewportCommand::Close → Closed
  Note over View,Eng: dropping the Shell joins the request workers, then the engine thread, the store's last reference drops and the data-root lock is released
